course: dictionary
lesson: 6154
title: Acting without words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mime is a way of telling a story with your body, your face and your hands, without saying a single word. When you read the word mime, look at the words around it for clues about what it means.
explain: «One mimed song on a TV show, where many performers mime, does not prove a singer cannot sing.» The words TV show and performers tell you this is about acting or performing. Mimed is a form of mime, so it must mean acting out a song without really singing it.
explain: Mime is also a noun, so a mime is a performer who acts this way, often with a white painted face. Mime can also be a verb, so to mime means to show something with actions instead of words.
fact: Mime means acting a story using only movements, faces and gestures.
fact: A mime is a performer who tells stories without words, often with a white painted face.
fact: To mime a song means to move your lips as if singing while a recording plays.
fact: In charades, players mime words or phrases for others to guess.
fact: Miming to a recording on a TV show is sometimes called cheating, because the singing is not live.
exercise: In drama class, Sam has to mime a cat washing itself. What does mime mean here? | *Show the action with movements and faces, not words | Speak loudly in a funny voice | Sing the song out loud | Draw a picture on paper
exercise: «The actor could not speak, so he mimed a message to the crowd.» How did he share the message? | He shouted it twice | *He used actions and gestures instead of words | Wrote it on a big board | He whispered it very quietly
exercise: «One mimed song on a TV show, where many performers mime, does not prove a singer cannot sing.» Find and copy one word that is a form of mime. | singer | sing | *mimed | prove
test: What is a mime artist? | A teacher who gives spelling tests | *A performer who tells a story using only movements and faces, often with a white painted face | A singer who records songs in a studio
test: When a singer mimes along to a recording, what are they doing? | *Moving their lips as if singing while the recording plays | Playing a guitar on stage | Writing new lyrics for the song | Singing live into a microphone
exam: In charades, Ruby must mime climbing a ladder, so what does she do? | Draws a ladder on the board | Shouts the word ladder | *Acts out climbing with her body and face, using no words | Climbs a real ladder in the hall
